# CIU machine-owned artifacts (S1.6/S1.7) — humans MUST NOT edit, MUST be gitignored
**/.ciu/

# Rendered config outputs (S1.8 — gitignored, see .gitignored.ciu)
ciu.global.toml
**/ciu.toml
# v8 design-set demo (docs/v8-dstdns-demo): in v8 `ciu.toml` is a COMMITTED
# declaration file (SPEC-V8 S2.1), so re-include the demo's copies that the v7
# rule above hides. Found 2026-09-03: the two earlier design-set commits shipped
# the demo without its ciu.toml because of this rule.
!docs/v8-dstdns-demo/ciu.toml
!docs/v8-dstdns-demo/examples/minimal/ciu.toml
# CIU's own rendered compose (a hand-written docker-compose.yml for the
# --shipped path is intentionally NOT ignored — maintainers commit it)
**/ciu.compose.yml
# The monorepo root .gitignore ignores **/docker-compose.yml globally; re-include
# it under ciu/ so a hand-written shipped compose (S8.5) stays committable.
!**/docker-compose.yml

# Per-stack override template `ciu.toml.j2`: COMMITTED, OPTIONAL sparse override
# (S3.1a, CIU-8). CIU never auto-creates it; like ciu.global.toml.j2 it is
# hand-authored, sparse, and tracked. Only the *rendered* ciu.toml (above) is
# gitignored — the override template is NOT.

# Workspace environment (machine identity layer, S2)
**/ciu.env

# Managed worktree identity/lifecycle record (S16) — machine-owned, per-checkout.
# Listed in `ciu init`'s canonical set since CIU-61 and in `.gitignored.ciu`,
# but genuinely absent from THIS file until ciu-P46's own `ciu migration-check`
# gitignore-gaps rule was pointed at ciu's own checkout and reported it. Kept as
# a real fix rather than silenced: it is exactly the omission that rule exists
# to catch, and CIU's own repo should be the first thing that satisfies it.
**/ciu.worktree-instance.json

# Per-checkout sparse global override (S3.1b) — declared gitignored by SPEC
# and by CIU's own published `.gitignored.ciu` sample rules, but missing here
# until CIU-60. Renamed from `ciu.global.worktree.toml.j2` by ciu-P47; the old
# spelling is dropped here as plain hygiene — it is no longer a CIU-generated
# artifact, so this repo has nothing to ignore under that name. It carries NO
# implication for `ciu migration-check`: that rule's retired-overlay detector
# is a bare filesystem existence check and never consults a `.gitignore`, so
# gitignore state and migration detection are independent (as
# `migration_check.detect_retired_overlay`'s own docstring and CONSUMERS §21
# both say).
**/ciu.global.instance.toml.j2

# CIU-owned generated identity facts (S3.1b), split out of the overlay above by
# ciu-P47. The integration suite generates into the committed `test-repo/`
# fixture, which would otherwise leave an untracked file that reds the
# dirty-tree gate (S18.4) on every run.
**/ciu.instance.generated.toml

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Build artifacts
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# setuptools-scm generated version file (written at build time)
src/ciu/_version.py

# Vendored Assay gate artifact (S18.1) — the released, hash-pinned zipapp is
# TRACKED, despite the monorepo root's `*.pyz` ignore (mirror of cmru's
# `!cmru/tools/assay/*.pyz`).
!tools/assay/*.pyz

# Controller checkpoint summary — a working-tree artifact, never committed.
# Gitignored (S18.4): the Assay-backed gate refuses a dirty tree, and an
# untracked non-ignored file here would otherwise red every gate run.
_last-summary.txt
